Lets the core have a page view stretch its last frame to fill it while it resizes, until the
renderer draws at the new size, rather than show it at its old size in the top-left corner. The
core turns it on while the app moves a page's left edge, as the sidebar hides or shows, so the
page's right edge and scrollbar stay still (issue #166). A hook only: the core decides when.

